invariant: INV-16
file: src/aead.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: aead_seal_cpu and aead_open_cpu never run the AVX-512 one pass, so a
  session whose ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA and the multiply bit
  seals a long record in two passes. Every byte is still right.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the one pass's calls at 2,085 bytes; the
  script builds it for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
        return n >= AEAD_AVX512_MIN ? ONE_PASS_AVX512 : ONE_PASS_NONE;
--- new
        return ONE_PASS_NONE;
